      <p><strong>Lennusadam Seaplane Harbour</strong> is one of Europe's finest maritime museums and one of Estonia's most popular attractions. It is housed inside historic seaplane hangars built between <strong>1916 and 1917</strong>. These remarkable reinforced-concrete structures were engineering masterpieces of their time and are now protected architectural monuments.</p>

